WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.317
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Are you
getting lots of questions

00:00:02.317 --> 00:00:04.320
from your customers
related to COVID-19?

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.630
In this video, I will
walk through the steps

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.065
to help you build and implement
a rapid response virtual agent.

00:00:10.065 --> 00:00:11.748
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:19.560
As the world responds
to the COVID-19 crisis,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.640
providing your
customers with accurate,

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.390
timely information
is crucial to keeping

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:26.400
people safe and informed.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.790
You can use the template in
this tutorial to set up a custom

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.240
rapid response voice and
chat virtual agent that

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:36.870
integrates directly into
your web, phone, social,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.070
and message channels.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:41.080
You can launch it in
23 different languages.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.190
And it's available for any
organization, including

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.640
health care and public
services, government agencies,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.310
and nonprofits, as well
as other industries that

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:54.180
are severely impacted, including
travel, financial services,

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.530
and retail.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.340
Let's take a look at how you can
get started using the template.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:03.180
Your first step is to download
the Dialogflow COVID-19 agent

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.480
template from GitHub
link in the description.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.340
To create the agent, navigate
to dialogflow.cloud.google.com,

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.400
log in, and click
Create New Agent.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:19.450
Give your agent a name,
and then click Create.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:22.300
Now, click on the gear
icon on the right-hand side

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:23.950
of the new agent.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.880
Under Export and Import,
select Import from ZIP,

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.390
and drop the ZIP file that you
just downloaded from GitHub.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:33.610
Now you're ready to
import and set up

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:35.320
the back end for your agent.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.040
And for that, you
deploy fulfillment.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.590
Go back to the GitHub and
download the Dialogflow

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.380
COVID-19 fulfillment.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.200
Back in the Dialogflow
console, click fulfillment

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.750
in the left sidebar
and toggle the switch

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:52.540
to enable the inline editor.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.930
You'll be asked to enable a
billing account in Google Cloud

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.100
console.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.590
When you're ready,
navigate to Cloud Functions

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:01.990
from the left panel.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:05.050
Under Source code, select
the ZIP upload, and upload

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.830
the ZIP file that
you got from GitHub.

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:18.230
Now you should see
three intents--

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:20.960
closure, confirmed
cases, and deaths.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:24.260
That requires setting up
Google Map's API and BigQuery

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.000
API for metrics.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Let's enable the
BigQuery API first.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.340
Select the APIs and services
from the left panel.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.320
Then click on Enable
APIs and services.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.750
Search for BigQuery
API and enable it.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.830
For the Maps API, you will
need to create credentials.

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.410
To do that, click
on Credentials.

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:49.130
Create credentials,
and then API key.

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:54.170
Make sure to restrict the key
to Cloud Functions API only.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.690
Now, back in our
Cloud Function, we

00:02:56.690 --> 00:03:00.590
need to set this API key
as an environment variable.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:03.320
For that, edit the
Cloud Function.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.430
Click on the environment
variables and add the variable.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:12.800
The name should be
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:17.090
And then the value should be
the API key you just created.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:19.220
And then just deploy.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.570
Now you're ready to test.

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:24.920
The easiest way to do that is
to test in Dialogflow simulator.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.600
Let's try an example.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.930
Is it still safe to
receive packages?

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.210
The response should
indicate that you set up

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:34.640
your agent correctly.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:37.430
If you plan on enabling
the bot on your website,

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:40.460
go to the integration
section on the left panel

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:43.310
and enable Dialogflow Messenger.

00:03:43.310 --> 00:03:46.830
Copy this code snippet and
add it to your website.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.800
You can also use the Try It
Now button to test it out.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.040
Let's say I select
Start Screening.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.130
The agent starts asking
me for specific symptoms

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:58.680
and directs me
based on my answers.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.850
If you want to enable this
experience via telephone,

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:06.290
go to the integrations, select
Dialogflow Phone Gateway

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:09.830
and a phone number.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:13.770
Place a call to the
number and test it out.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.480
If you want to interact
with the Dialogflow API,

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.540
you will need to create
a service account

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.850
and download the private key.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.410
Here's how you would do that.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.830
Go to the IAM in admin
on the left panel

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.170
and select Service Accounts.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.840
Create a new service account.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:33.300
Give your new account a name.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.970
The role would be project owner.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:38.910
And then click
Create, Create Key

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:42.360
will let you download the
JSON key on your computer.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:45.070
You will use this file
in your environment.

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.960
So save it.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.340
Open the terminal on
your local machine

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:53.980
or any other interface where
you can run a call command.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:58.260
Execute export Google
application credentials,

00:04:58.260 --> 00:05:02.090
which would be equal to the
location of your key file

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:04.310
in quotations.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.710
So make sure you provide
the right location.

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:09.890
To test, we will
need a user request.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:14.210
Let's say the user asks,
how can I get tested.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.860
We put that in a file
called request.JSON.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:20.960
And next, we will
send this request

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.250
to Dialogflow detect intent
API using the code command

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.280
with post request
option authorization

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.850
header that gets the token
value via gcloud auth command.

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:37.540
And then, the data gets
parsed as request.JSON.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:40.720
And there you have a
response in JSON format.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:42.580
All that's left
is to parse it out

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:47.300
and do what you need to do with
it in your custom application.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.890
[? Current ?] is
just an example.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:50.530
You can interact
with the Dialogflow

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.140
API using other
language integrations,

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.050
like Python, Java, et cetera.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.920
Refer to the
documentation linked below

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.200
for language of your choice.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.250
And that's it.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.520
We hope you and your customers
will find the Rapid Response

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:06.580
Virtual Agent helpful during
this unprecedented time.

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:09.030
[MUSIC PLAYING]

